const ROWS = [{"surface": "Menus, keys, startup and quit", "file": "menus-and-app.md", "section": "Inventory", "n": "1", "site": "GUI_App:5311-5321 (`import_model` picker), called from Plater:19078-19085 (`add_file`, Win/Linux) and Plater:16705-16713 (`add_model`, Mac)", "gist": "File picker \"Choose one or more files (3MF/STEP/STL/SVG/OBJ/AMF…)\"", "trigger": "File › Import › Import 3MF/STL/STEP/SVG/OBJ/AMF…; Ctrl/Cmd+I while a project is showing", "condition": "Always", "reach": "yes", "reachNote": "**yes**. AppMenus keeps the item and only removes its picture (AppMenus.cpp:413-420). **Suspected bug:** the picker opens inside the `FileOpenScope` at Plater:19080/16707, so the open's least-change listener is active. Since 3aa5a4435d the listener sees native pickers (wx `filedlg.mm:599`, `msw/filedlg.cpp:1249` and `gtk/filedlg.cpp:434` call `WX_HOOK_MODAL_DIALOG`). A picker has no wx buttons, so `least_change_answer` returns Cancel (DialogListeners.cpp:169-173). My reading is that the picker is cancelled before it ever shows. Not run. Home's Open… is not affected: it opens the picker before any scope (OrcaHomeBackend.cpp:1458-1469).", "route": "SHOW", "routeNote": "SHOW"}, {"surface": "Menus, keys, startup and quit", "file": "menus-and-app.md", "section": "Inventory", "n": "2", "site": "GUI_App:5326-5332 (`import_zip`), from Plater:18187-18197", "gist": "File picker \"Choose ZIP file:\"", "trigger": "File › Import › Import ZIP Archive…", "condition": "Not on Home (AppMenus.cpp:417-419)", "reach": "yes", "reachNote": "**yes**. The picker opens outside any scope.", "route": "SHOW", "routeNote": "SHOW"}, {"surface": "Menus, keys, startup and quit", "file": "menus-and-app.md", "section": "Inventory", "n": "3", "site": "Plater:18518-18519 (`FileArchiveDialog` in `preview_zip_archive`); ZIP errors `show_error` Plater:18565, 18575, 18616", "gist": "ZIP contents chooser (Open/Cancel); \"Loading of a ZIP archive on path … has failed.\"", "trigger": "After row 2, or a .zip dropped on Prepare or opened from the OS", "condition": "The file is a .zip", "reach": "yes", "reachNote": "**yes**. **Suspected bug:** it runs inside `Plater::load_files`'s `FileOpenScope` (Plater:18834) with `prefer_cancel`, and the dialog has a `wxID_CANCEL` button (FileArchiveDialog.cpp:417). My reading is that it is answered Cancel, so nothing is imported. Not run.", "route": "SHOW", "routeNote": "SHOW (chooser); errors stay ANSWER as today"}, {"surface": "Menus, keys, startup and quit", "file": "menus-and-app.md", "section": "Inventory", "n": "4", "site": "Plater:9280 (3MF version and origin infos), 9308 (2.3.1-alpha rotate template), 9598 and 9611 (modified G-code / customized preset warnings), 9822 (STEP not UTF-8), 9835 (`StepMeshDialog`), 9904 and 9908 (load failure), 9927 (zero volume), 9934 and 9942 (object too small, scale?), 9974 (multi-part?), 10054 (texture fallback), 10113 (single object with parts?), 10170 (sync printer, suppressed by setting), 10321 (no geometry), 10376 and 10388 (object too large), 15746 (`normalize_bed_types`), 18860, 18868 and 18924 (G-code infos), 6040 (gcode.3mf warning), 19013 (`ProjectDropDialog`, suppressed by setting)", "gist": "OrcaSlicer's questions and notices while a file loads", "trigger": "Import, Finder or Explorer open, a second launch handing over a file, a drop on Prepare, Home's Open or drop", "condition": "Depends on the file", "reach": "yes", "reachNote": "**yes**, already answered with the least change and reported to the AI (OrcaWorkspaceAdapter.cpp:572-579 and 668-760). The answer is chosen from the buttons alone, so \"too small, scale to mm?\" gets No, \"single object?\" gets No, \"too large\" (lone Yes) gets Yes, and STEP settings get OK.", "route": "ANSWER", "routeNote": "ANSWER (covered)"}, {"surface": "Menus, keys, startup and quit", "file": "menus-and-app.md", "section": "Inventory", "n": "5", "site": "Plater:19764-19777 (save picker, then \"The provided file name is not valid…\" `show_error` and the picker again)", "gist": "\"Save G-code file as:\"", "trigger": "File › Export › Export G-code…; the header's Export (StatusRow.cpp:627-630); the export notification's link (Plater:8313 → `export_gcode(true)`)", "condition": "Plate sliced", "reach": "yes", "reachNote": "**yes** **Correction from a later trace:** the export notification's link never shows in the JusPrin view, because OrcaSlicer's notifications are not drawn there.", "route": "SHOW", "routeNote": "SHOW"}, {"surface": "Menus, keys, startup and quit", "file": "menus-and-app.md", "section": "Inventory", "n": "6", "site": "Plater:19742 and 19745 (`show_error` from placeholder or config errors), 11692 and 11724 (\"Another export job is running.\")", "gist": "Errors before or while exporting", "trigger": "Same as row 5", "condition": "Bad output-name template, or a second export while one runs", "reach": "yes", "reachNote": "**yes**", "route": "JUSPRIN-MESSAGE", "routeNote": "JUSPRIN-MESSAGE"}, {"surface": "Menus, keys, startup and quit", "file": "menus-and-app.md", "section": "Inventory", "n": "7", "site": "MainFrame:694-760 → Plater:19431 (\"The current project has unsaved changes…\") and GUI_App:9325 (`UnsavedChangesDialog`)", "gist": "Save-or-discard and preset transfer-or-discard on quit", "trigger": "File › Quit/Exit, Cmd/Ctrl+Q, Mac app-menu Quit (MainFrame:3864-3871), Dock quit and OS logout (GUI_App:3263-3276)", "condition": "Project or presets modified", "reach": "no", "reachNote": "**no**. Settled by the before-release hook.", "route": "ANSWER", "routeNote": "ANSWER (covered)"}, {"surface": "Menus, keys, startup and quit", "file": "menus-and-app.md", "section": "Inventory", "n": "8", "site": "GUI_App:9455-9478 (`check_print_host_queue`)", "gist": "\"Ongoing uploads\": \"The uploads are still ongoing … Stop them and continue anyway?\"", "trigger": "Any quit (MainFrame:719)", "condition": "A send to a Moonraker or OctoPrint host is still uploading", "reach": "yes", "reachNote": "**yes**. The before-re